.TH OTPME-DEVICE 1 "2026" "OTPme" "OTPme Manual"
.SH NAME
otpme-device \- manage OTPme network devices for MAB port authentication
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B otpme-device
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIdevice\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B otpme-device
manages network devices in the OTPme system. Devices represent network
equipment such as IP phones or printers that authenticate via MAC
Authentication Bypass (MAB). Each device has a MAC address and can be
assigned to an access group to control network access.
.PP
To use a device for MAB port authentication, add it with
.BR otpme-device ,
set its MAC address and add it to the appropriate access group with
.BR otpme-accessgroup (1).
A VLAN can be assigned on top of that, see
.B VLAN Assignment
below.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Device Management
.TP
.B add \fIdevice\fR
Create a new device.
.TP
.B del \fIdevice\fR
Delete a device.
.TP
.B show \fR[\fIdevice\fR]
Display device information.
.TP
.B list \fR[\fIregex\fR]
List devices, optionally filtered by regex pattern.
.TP
.B enable \fIdevice\fR
Enable a disabled device.
.TP
.B disable \fIdevice\fR
Disable a device without deleting it.
.TP
.B touch \fIdevice\fR
Re-index the device to fix potential index problems.
.TP
.B move \fR[\fB\-\-keep\-acls\fR] \fIdevice\fR \fIunit\fR
Move device to a different unit.
.TP
.B auto_disable \fR[\fB\-u\fR] \fIdevice\fR \fItime\fR
Set auto\-disable time.
It is either a relative time with a leading \fB+\fR, e.g. \fB+30D\fR, or an absolute one, e.g. \fB"09:53 13.06.2023"\fR.
The units are \fBs\fR, \fBm\fR, \fBh\fR, \fBD\fR, \fBW\fR, \fBM\fR and \fBY\fR, see
.BR otpme (7).
Use \fB\-u\fR to disable the object if it was unused for the given time.
.SS MAC Address
.TP
.B mac \fIdevice\fR \fImac_address\fR
Set the MAC address of the device. The MAC address is used for MAB port
authentication.
.SS VLAN Assignment
A device is not assigned a VLAN from here. Either the VLAN names the device,
so that the assignment belongs to the site that runs the network (see
.BR otpme-vlan (1)):
.PP
.RS
.B otpme-vlan add_device \fIvlan\fR \fIdevice\fR
.RE
.PP
or the device names the VLAN through its
.B vlans
config parameter (see
.BR otpme (7)):
.PP
.RS
.B otpme-device config \fIdevice\fR vlans \fIvlan\fR
.RE
.PP
The VLAN is returned during MAB port authentication, together with the
access granted through the access group. Membership wins: the
.B vlans
parameter is only looked at when no VLAN of the site answering the RADIUS
request names the device. A device that is in a VLAN only through a role is
overridden by one that names the device itself.
.SS Configuration
.TP
.B config \fR[\fB\-d\fR] [\fB\-a\fR] \fIdevice\fR \fIparameter\fR \fR[\fIvalue\fR]
Set a configuration parameter. Use \fB\-d\fR to delete (reset to
default), \fB\-a\fR to append a value.
.TP
.B show_config \fIdevice\fR [\fIparameter\fR]
Show all configuration parameters.
.TP
.B get_config \fIdevice\fR \fIparameter\fR
Show the value of a single configuration parameter.
.TP
.B description \fIdevice\fR \fR[\fIdescription\fR]
Set device description.
.TP
.B info \fR[\fB\-\-language\fR \fILANG\fR] \fIdevice\fR \fR[\fIinfo\fR]
Set free-form info text. If \fIinfo\fR is omitted, the current info text is
opened in the editor specified by the \fBEDITOR\fR environment variable.
.TP
.B dump_info \fR[\fB\-\-language\fR \fILANG\fR] \fIdevice\fR
Dump the info text to stdout.
.SS Object Changelog
Every change to the object writes an entry: who made it, when, and what was done.
A change can carry a comment of its own, through the global option \fB\-\-changelog\fR.
.PP
An \fIentry_id\fR is the number the listing shows in front of an entry, counted from 0.
.PP
Only the comment of an entry can be changed or removed.
What was done and by whom stays as it is.
.PP
A command that changes something asks first; the global option \fB\-f\fR skips the question.
.TP
.B changelog \fIdevice\fR
Show the changelog of the device.
Needs the ACL \fBview:changelog\fR.
.TP
.B edit_changelog \fIdevice\fR \fIentry_id\fR \fIcomment\fR
Set the comment of that entry, or replace the one it has.
Needs the ACL \fBedit:changelog\fR.
.TP
.B del_changelog \fIdevice\fR \fIentry_id\fR
Remove the comment of that entry.
The entry itself stays, and an entry without a comment is refused.
Needs the ACL \fBedit:changelog\fR.
.TP
.B clear_changelog \fIdevice\fR
Remove every entry of the changelog.
.br
This needs more than the ACL \fBclear:changelog\fR: the config parameter
.B allow_changelog_clearing
has to allow it (see \fBotpme\fR(7)).
It is true by default, but where no value is found at all, clearing is refused.
OTPme asks the token you are signed in with first, then the object.
.SS Policy Management
A \fIpolicy\fR is the name of a policy, not a path.
It is looked for in the site of the device.
Which policies there are, and what each of them does, is in
.BR otpme\-policy (1).
.PP
Attaching and detaching ask before they change anything; the global option \fB\-f\fR skips the question.
.TP
.B add_policy \fIdevice\fR \fIpolicy\fR
Attach a policy to the device.
.br
A policy has a list of object types it is for; one that does not name \fBdevice\fR is refused.
So is a second policy of a type that allows only one per object.
.br
Needs the ACL \fBassign:policy\fR.
.TP
.B remove_policy \fIdevice\fR \fIpolicy\fR
Remove a policy from the device.
.br
Needs the ACL \fBremove:policy\fR, and that one verbatim: a plain \fBremove\fR does not cover it.
Detaching a policy takes away what it enforces, so it must not be cheaper than attaching one.
.TP
.B list_policies \fR[\fB\-\-return\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] [\fB\-\-policy\-types\fR \fIt1,t2\fR] \fIdevice\fR
List the policies attached to the device.
Use \fB\-\-return\-type\fR to select the attribute returned (\fBname\fR, \fBread_oid\fR, \fBfull_oid\fR, \fBuuid\fR).
Use \fB\-\-policy\-types\fR to list only policies of the given types; these are policy types, not policy names.
.br
Needs the ACL \fBview:policies\fR.
.SS ACL Management
.TP
.B add_acl \fIdevice\fR \fIowner_type\fR \fIowner\fR \fIacl\fR
Add an access control entry.
.TP
.B del_acl \fIdevice\fR \fIacl\fR
Remove an access control entry.
.TP
.B list_acls \fIdevice\fR
Display all ACLs for the device.
.TP
.B enable_acl_inheritance \fIdevice\fR
Enable ACL inheritance from parent objects.
.TP
.B disable_acl_inheritance \fIdevice\fR
Disable ACL inheritance.
.SS Import/Export
.TP
.B export \fR[\fB\-\-password\fR \fIPASS\fR] \fIdevice\fR
Export device configuration.
.TP
.B remove_orphans \fIdevice\fR
Remove orphaned object references.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Display Options
.TP
.B \-a
Show all devices (across all units).
.TP
.B \-z \fISIZE\fR
Limit output size.
.TP
.B \-\-fields \fIFIELD1,FIELD2\fR
Display only specified fields.
.TP
.B \-\-policy\-limit \fIN\fR
Limit number of policies shown.
.TP
.B \-\-limit \fIN\fR
Limit number of items shown per object.
.TP
.TP
.B \-\-sort\-by \fIFIELD\fR
Sort output by field.
.TP
.B \-\-reverse
Reverse sort order.
.TP
.B \-\-raw
Output without headers/borders.
.TP
.B \-\-csv
Output as CSV.
.TP
.B \-\-csv\-sep \fISEP\fR
CSV separator character.
.TP
.B \-\-attribute \fIATTR\fR
Display specific attribute in list command.
.SS General Options
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-acls
Preserve ACLs when moving device.
.TP
.B \-\-password \fIPASS\fR
Password for encrypting exports.
.PP
Global options are available for all commands. See
.BR otpme (1)
for details.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B otpme-device add ip-phone-1
Create a device for an IP phone
.TP
.B otpme-device mac ip-phone-1 90:1b:0e:46:46:15
Set the MAC address
.TP
.B otpme-accessgroup add_device lan ip-phone-1
Add device to access group for MAB
.TP
.B otpme-vlan add_device voice ip-phone-1
Put the device into the voice VLAN
.TP
.B otpme-device description ip-phone-1 "Reception IP Phone"
Set description
.TP
.B otpme-device show ip-phone-1
Show device details
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/otpme/
OTPme data directory
